    {
     "type": "application",
     "title": "Run a Daily Control Audit",
     "content": "Epictetus's students didn't just read the dichotomy of control — they drilled it, the way you'd drill a muscle. Here's a version you can run in under ten minutes a day.\n\n1. **Write down today's obstacle** in one sentence, as concretely as possible — not 'my career' but 'the rejection email I got this morning.'\n\n2. **Split it into two columns**: what is genuinely up to you (your response, effort, judgment, next action) and what is not (the decision itself, other people's opinions, timing, luck).\n\n3. **Cross out the second column entirely.** Not ignore it — cross it out. You are not responsible for producing outcomes there, only for how you engage.\n\n4. **Write one sentence of action** that lives entirely in the first column — something you can do today regardless of how the uncontrollable column resolves.\n\n5. **Do an evening review**, the way Marcus Aurelius did nightly: did you spend energy today on the crossed-out column? Note it, without self-punishment, and adjust tomorrow.\n\nThis is the actual mechanism Stockdale used under far worse conditions than yours. It is not a metaphor. It is a procedure. Run it for a full week before judging whether it works — a single day rarely reveals whether you are actually catching yourself mid-complaint about the column you already crossed out.",
     "visual": {
      "type": "diagram",
      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"32\">YOUR CONTROL AUDIT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">A ten-minute daily drill</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"150\" width=\"800\" height=\"115\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#ffd700\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"195\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">1. NAME THE OBSTACLE</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"235\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">One sentence, as concrete as possible</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"280\" width=\"800\" height=\"115\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"325\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">2. SPLIT THE COLUMNS</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"365\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">Up to you vs. not up to you</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"410\" width=\"800\" height=\"115\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"455\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">3. CROSS OUT COLUMN TWO</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"495\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">Not ignored -- released</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"540\" width=\"800\" height=\"115\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#0ea5e9\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"585\" fill=\"#0ea5e9\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">4. WRITE ONE ACTION</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"625\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">Living entirely in column one</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"670\" width=\"800\" height=\"115\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"715\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"21\">5. RUN AN EVENING REVIEW</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"755\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"14\">Marcus Aurelius's own nightly habit</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"825\" width=\"700\" height=\"110\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#ffd700\" fill-opacity=\"0.1\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"890\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"20\">The exact procedure Stockdale used under torture.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "A ten-minute daily drill in the dichotomy of control."
     }
    }
