      "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"32\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"95\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Amor fati vs. Stoic acceptance</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"150\" width=\"940\" height=\"250\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#6366f1\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"205\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">THE CONCEPT TESTED</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"250\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">Two different grounds for saying yes to fate.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"285\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">One rational and cosmic, one willed and individual.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"325\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"15\">The word 'amor fati' hides this split.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"430\" width=\"940\" height=\"250\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#ef4444\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">THE COMMON MISCONCEPTION</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"530\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">Treating amor fati as just a synonym for Stoicism.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"565\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">Assuming Holiday's usage matches Nietzsche's own.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"605\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"15\">The two philosophers would have disagreed sharply.</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"710\" width=\"940\" height=\"250\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"#10b981\" fill-opacity=\"0.12\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"765\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"23\">REMEMBER</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"810\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">Stoics: reason already endorses your fate.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"845\" fill=\"#ffffff\" font-size=\"18\">Nietzsche: you alone must choose to endorse it.</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"885\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"15\">Same yes, two very different reasons for it.</text></svg>",
      "caption": "Separating two philosophies sharing one phrase."
