     "explanation": "Epictetus's prohairesis is a stable faculty of judgment and choice that Stoic practice deliberately strengthens. Zen, drawing on the Buddhist doctrine of anatta, treats the very idea of a fixed, separate self facing its circumstances as a construction to be seen through, which is why Zen practice aims at loosening self-identification rather than fortifying a sovereign will.",
